how to set 192.168.10.1 on the Raspberry Pi, because that's the part that's probably confusing you.??

On the Raspberry Pi

Open Terminal and run:

sudo nmcli connection show

Look for the Ethernet connection, usually something like Wired connection 1.

Then run:

sudo nmcli connection modify "Wired connection 1" ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses 192.168.10.1/24 ipv4.gateway "" ipv4.dns ""

Then activate it:

sudo nmcli connection up "Wired connection 1"

Finally, check:

ip addr show eth0

You should see:

inet 192.168.10.1/24
Then your final IP setup is:
PC1 — Raspberry Pi
IP: 192.168.10.1
Mask: 255.255.255.0

        Ethernet cable

PC2 — Windows
IP: 192.168.10.2
Mask: 255.255.255.0

Don't run the commands yet if your connection isn't actually named Wired connection 1. First run:

sudo nmcli connection show

